#%PAM-1.0
# hyprlock's PASSWORD path. Install: sudo install -m 644 this /etc/pam.d/
#
# system-auth without `auth sufficient pam_fprintd.so` and without faillock.
#
# No pam_fprintd: hyprlock reads the fingerprint itself, over fprintd's D-Bus
# API, AT THE SAME TIME as the password field. If this stack also asked
# pam_fprintd, a typed password would wait for a finger — the swaylock problem.
#
# No pam_faillock: when the FINGER unlocks, hyprlock cancels the pending
# password conversation and faillock records that as a failed login. Three
# finger unlocks in 15 min would then lock the password (login, sudo) for
# 10 min. pam_unix still delays each wrong password.

-auth      [success=1 default=ignore]  pam_systemd_home.so
auth       required                    pam_unix.so          try_first_pass nullok
auth       required                    pam_env.so

account    include                     system-auth
